## Override: the common standard.list.chroot pulls the Debian "standard"
## priority set (via `! Packages Priority standard`), which includes
## openssh-client. Since kali-linux-core depends on kali-system-core which
## requires openssh-client-gssapi (Conflicts: openssh-client), the standard
## set creates an unresolvable apt conflict in Kali rolling.
##
## The shadow variant explicitly lists all required packages in
## kali.list.chroot, so the implicit standard set is not needed.
##
## This override replaces the common file for the shadow variant only;
## other variants are unaffected.
